  "worked_solution": "First, let's compute the *squared* distance $S(a)$ between the two points. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S(a) & =(a+1-1)^{2}+(a-(-2))^{2} \\\\  & =(a)^{2}+(a+2)^{2} \\\\  & ={a}^{2}+{a}^{2}+4a+4 \\\\  & =2{a}^{2}+4a+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want to minimize $S,$ we compute the derivative ${S}^{\u2032}(a).$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}^{\u2032}(a) & =4a+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe stationary points of $S(a)$ are the points where the derivative ${S}^{\u2032}(a)=0.$ Solving this equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}^{\u2032}(a) & =0 \\\\ 4a+4 & =0 \\\\ a & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can see that ${S}^{\u2033}(-1)=4>0.$ Therefore, the squared distance (and therefore the actual distance) reaches a minimum when $a=-1.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
